1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:04,182
Most test day problems have
nothing to do with math or grammar.

2
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:05,718
A missing ID.

3
00:00:05,861 --> 00:00:07,162
A dead laptop.

4
00:00:07,182 --> 00:00:09,090
A phone that buzzes in a bag.

5
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:12,555
This video walks through the
whole SAT test day in order,

6
00:00:12,575 --> 00:00:14,484
from packing your bag
to getting your scores,

7
00:00:14,504 --> 00:00:16,356
so nothing catches you off guard.

8
00:00:16,376 --> 00:00:21,285
The rules and times in this video come
from College Board's own test day pages.

9
00:00:21,305 --> 00:00:24,142
The pacing and reset tips are advice,

10
00:00:24,162 --> 00:00:25,249
not rules.

11
00:00:25,269 --> 00:00:29,212
Details can change, so give those
pages a quick look before your test,

12
00:00:29,232 --> 00:00:29,937
too.

13
00:00:29,957 --> 00:00:31,330
Start with the must-bring list.

14
00:00:31,350 --> 00:00:35,993
Your testing device, fully charged, with
Bluebook installed and exam setup done.

15
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:40,009
Exam setup happens in Bluebook
one to five days before the test,

16
00:00:40,029 --> 00:00:42,417
and it's what gives you
your admission ticket.

17
00:00:42,437 --> 00:00:44,844
Next, your up-to-date admission ticket.

18
00:00:44,864 --> 00:00:47,738
College Board says a
printed ticket is preferred.

19
00:00:47,758 --> 00:00:51,988
Then an acceptable photo ID,
pencils or pens for scratch work,

20
00:00:52,008 --> 00:00:54,523
and your College Board
username and password,

21
00:00:54,543 --> 00:00:56,758
because you'll sign in at the test center.

22
00:00:56,785 --> 00:00:59,551
Your ID is where students get turned away.

23
00:00:59,571 --> 00:01:03,122
It has to be a physical ID,
not a photo on your phone,

24
00:01:03,142 --> 00:01:04,964
and it can't be expired.

25
00:01:04,999 --> 00:01:09,229
A driver's license, a passport, or an
ID from the school you attend now can

26
00:01:09,249 --> 00:01:09,979
work.

27
00:01:09,999 --> 00:01:11,883
Temporary IDs don't.

28
00:01:11,903 --> 00:01:15,097
The name on it has to match
your admission ticket exactly.

29
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:19,239
College Board's own example: you can't
use a nickname on one and your full name

30
00:01:19,259 --> 00:01:20,097
on the other.

31
00:01:20,117 --> 00:01:24,347
And if you forget your ID, staff don't
have to hold your seat while you go get

32
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:24,787
it.

33
00:01:24,807 --> 00:01:26,343
About calculators.

34
00:01:27,021 --> 00:01:30,787
College Board's bring list
includes an acceptable calculator,

35
00:01:30,807 --> 00:01:34,180
but Bluebook has a Desmos
calculator built in,

36
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:38,492
and College Board's calculator policy
says calculators aren't required.

37
00:01:38,512 --> 00:01:40,849
If you bring your own, it
has to be an approved model,

38
00:01:40,869 --> 00:01:44,599
and calculators with a computer
algebra system aren't allowed.

39
00:01:44,619 --> 00:01:47,011
Bring one you already know, not a new one.

40
00:01:47,066 --> 00:01:50,689
Nice to have: a charging
cable or portable charger,

41
00:01:50,709 --> 00:01:55,209
a watch with no audible alarm,
a drink or snack for the break,

42
00:01:55,244 --> 00:01:58,030
a bag, and a backup
device if you have one.

43
00:01:58,102 --> 00:02:01,082
College Board recommends the
charger but can't promise an outlet,

44
00:02:01,102 --> 00:02:03,604
so charge fully the night before anyway.

45
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:06,568
Now what stays home,
or at least stays off.

46
00:02:06,588 --> 00:02:08,890
Phones, smartwatches, fitness trackers,

47
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:13,338
wireless earbuds, separate timers, and
any notes or books are all prohibited.

48
00:02:13,358 --> 00:02:17,196
If you bring your phone, staff will either
collect it or have you put it in your

49
00:02:17,216 --> 00:02:20,445
bag away from your desk,
and that includes breaks.

50
00:02:20,465 --> 00:02:23,696
And if a prohibited device makes noise,

51
00:02:23,716 --> 00:02:26,088
or you're seen with it, even on a break,

52
00:02:26,108 --> 00:02:28,981
you can be dismissed and
your scores can be canceled.

53
00:02:29,001 --> 00:02:31,022
That's a lot to risk for a phone.

54
00:02:31,042 --> 00:02:32,451
Test morning.

55
00:02:32,471 --> 00:02:35,379
Close and reopen Bluebook
before you leave.

56
00:02:35,399 --> 00:02:39,308
College Board says that's how you check
for last-minute messages and updated

57
00:02:39,328 --> 00:02:40,863
test center information.

58
00:02:40,951 --> 00:02:44,038
Test centers open at 7:45 in the morning,

59
00:02:44,058 --> 00:02:48,002
and doors close at eight, unless
your admission ticket says otherwise.

60
00:02:48,022 --> 00:02:50,358
If you're borrowing a
device from College Board,

61
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:52,395
arrive at 7:15.

62
00:02:52,415 --> 00:02:56,220
Testing usually starts between
eight fifteen and eight thirty.

63
00:02:56,240 --> 00:03:00,026
In the testing room, the proctor
checks your ID and checks you in.

64
00:03:00,062 --> 00:03:01,562
Your seat is assigned.

65
00:03:01,776 --> 00:03:04,097
You'll connect to the center's Wi-Fi,

66
00:03:04,169 --> 00:03:07,613
open Bluebook, sign in, and
follow the check-in steps,

67
00:03:07,633 --> 00:03:09,669
which include clearing your desk.

68
00:03:09,738 --> 00:03:13,110
The proctor reads a short script,
collects any devices that aren't allowed,

69
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:14,738
and gives you a start code.

70
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:16,967
Scratch paper comes
from the testing staff,

71
00:03:16,987 --> 00:03:18,631
and they collect it at the end.

72
00:03:18,808 --> 00:03:21,238
Enter the start code, and the test begins.

73
00:03:21,264 --> 00:03:23,243
Before the first
question, know your tools.

74
00:03:23,263 --> 00:03:26,708
You can try all of them ahead of
time in Bluebook's test preview,

75
00:03:26,728 --> 00:03:31,121
which is untimed, so none of
this should be new on test day.

76
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:33,588
At the top, there's a timer
for each part of the test.

77
00:03:33,608 --> 00:03:37,375
You can hide it, and Bluebook
alerts you when five minutes remain.

78
00:03:37,395 --> 00:03:41,679
If the clock makes you anxious, hide
it and check it at set points instead.

79
00:03:41,710 --> 00:03:45,548
Mark for review puts a bookmark on
any question you want to come back to.

80
00:03:45,568 --> 00:03:48,975
The option eliminator lets you cross
out choices you think are wrong,

81
00:03:48,995 --> 00:03:50,225
and you can undo it.

82
00:03:50,245 --> 00:03:54,318
Highlights and notes let you highlight
text or leave yourself a note.

83
00:03:54,373 --> 00:03:56,674
On math, you get the Desmos calculator,

84
00:03:56,694 --> 00:03:58,710
which you can drag anywhere on the screen,

85
00:03:58,730 --> 00:04:01,389
and a reference sheet of common formulas.

86
00:04:01,409 --> 00:04:06,852
There's also a line reader, zoom, and a
question menu that shows which questions

87
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:09,766
you skipped or marked, so you
can jump straight to them.

88
00:04:09,825 --> 00:04:12,019
The first section is Reading and Writing.

89
00:04:12,039 --> 00:04:14,627
It's two modules of
thirty-two minutes each,

90
00:04:14,647 --> 00:04:17,039
with twenty-seven questions per module.

91
00:04:17,181 --> 00:04:19,727
That's about seventy-one
seconds a question.

92
00:04:19,747 --> 00:04:22,655
A simple checkpoint: when half
the module's time is gone,

93
00:04:22,675 --> 00:04:24,798
you want to be around question fourteen.

94
00:04:24,818 --> 00:04:28,940
If you're well behind that, stop
rereading every passage twice.

95
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,987
Mark the hard ones and keep moving.

96
00:04:31,007 --> 00:04:35,273
Inside a module, you can move back and
forth and return to anything you marked.

97
00:04:35,293 --> 00:04:38,542
But once you move on from a
module, you can't go back to it.

98
00:04:38,649 --> 00:04:43,486
So before time runs out, open the question
menu and make sure every question has

99
00:04:43,506 --> 00:04:44,401
an answer.

100
00:04:44,421 --> 00:04:45,528
Why no blanks?

101
00:04:45,814 --> 00:04:48,294
College Board says there's
no penalty for guessing,

102
00:04:48,314 --> 00:04:51,329
and that it's better to guess
than leave a question blank.

103
00:04:51,349 --> 00:04:53,937
Eliminate what you can,
pick from what's left,

104
00:04:53,957 --> 00:04:54,943
and move on.

105
00:04:54,963 --> 00:04:57,193
Then module two starts.

106
00:04:57,213 --> 00:05:00,228
There's no scheduled
break between modules.

107
00:05:00,248 --> 00:05:05,674
Each module is timed separately, so
module two gets its own full clock.

108
00:05:05,694 --> 00:05:10,317
Module two is harder or easier
depending on how you did in module one.

109
00:05:10,337 --> 00:05:11,995
Don't try to figure out which one you got.

110
00:05:12,015 --> 00:05:15,173
If it feels hard, that can
mean module one went well.

111
00:05:15,193 --> 00:05:18,514
Either way, the only thing that
helps now is the next question.

112
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:22,382
If module one felt rough,
reset before you start.

113
00:05:22,417 --> 00:05:23,933
Take one slow breath.

114
00:05:23,953 --> 00:05:25,718
Put your pencil down for a second.

115
00:05:25,738 --> 00:05:29,147
Then read the first question of module
two like it's the first question of the

116
00:05:29,167 --> 00:05:29,897
day.

117
00:05:29,917 --> 00:05:32,218
Your section score counts both modules,

118
00:05:32,238 --> 00:05:34,989
so one rough module doesn't decide it.

119
00:05:35,048 --> 00:05:37,634
After Reading and Writing
comes the one scheduled break:

120
00:05:37,654 --> 00:05:38,706
ten minutes.

121
00:05:38,726 --> 00:05:40,063
Leave your device open.

122
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:41,242
Don't close it.

123
00:05:41,262 --> 00:05:43,618
And keep your ID with you the whole time.

124
00:05:43,654 --> 00:05:44,384
Use the break.

125
00:05:44,404 --> 00:05:47,920
Eat your snack, drink some
water, stand up and stretch.

126
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:50,313
Your phone stays off-limits, even now,

127
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:53,384
and if you brought a calculator,
it stays on your desk.

128
00:05:53,404 --> 00:05:57,598
And don't spend the break replaying
Reading and Writing questions.

129
00:05:57,618 --> 00:05:59,134
That section is done.

130
00:05:59,154 --> 00:06:01,011
Math is the only thing left.

131
00:06:01,049 --> 00:06:04,101
You can take an extra, unscheduled
break if you really need one.

132
00:06:04,121 --> 00:06:07,199
But you'll lose testing time,
so save it for a real emergency.

133
00:06:07,219 --> 00:06:09,198
The second section is Math.

134
00:06:09,218 --> 00:06:11,306
Two modules of thirty-five minutes each,

135
00:06:11,326 --> 00:06:13,699
with twenty-two questions per module.

136
00:06:13,719 --> 00:06:16,362
That's about ninety-five
seconds a question.

137
00:06:16,433 --> 00:06:21,112
Most are multiple choice, and some
ask you to type in your own answer.

138
00:06:21,135 --> 00:06:25,385
At an even pace, you'd reach question
eleven when half the time is gone.

139
00:06:25,635 --> 00:06:28,150
Math questions go from easiest to hardest,

140
00:06:28,170 --> 00:06:29,829
so try to be a little ahead of that.

141
00:06:29,849 --> 00:06:33,813
If a question has eaten about two
minutes and you still don't have a plan,

142
00:06:33,919 --> 00:06:36,670
mark it, guess, and come
back if there's time.

143
00:06:36,695 --> 00:06:40,283
Use Desmos where it's faster:
finding where two graphs cross,

144
00:06:40,303 --> 00:06:44,389
finding x intercepts, and checking
an answer you got by hand.

145
00:06:44,409 --> 00:06:46,890
And on questions where
you type the answer,

146
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:50,088
reread what the question
asks for before you enter it.

147
00:06:50,135 --> 00:06:52,794
If you finish a module early,
there's no prize for that.

148
00:06:52,814 --> 00:06:54,901
You can't submit the test early anyway.

149
00:06:54,921 --> 00:06:57,471
So spend the extra time
on your marked questions,

150
00:06:57,491 --> 00:07:01,294
then recheck anything where you might
have dropped a sign or misread the

151
00:07:01,314 --> 00:07:02,167
question.

152
00:07:02,187 --> 00:07:06,096
When the test ends, your answers
are submitted automatically.

153
00:07:06,116 --> 00:07:10,810
Don't close your device or turn off the
screen until you see the Congratulations

154
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:11,565
screen.

155
00:07:11,585 --> 00:07:14,049
If the submission fails, don't panic.

156
00:07:14,084 --> 00:07:16,065
Your answers are saved to your device,

157
00:07:16,085 --> 00:07:19,351
and you have until the end
of the next day to resubmit.

158
00:07:19,371 --> 00:07:21,636
Then the proctor collects
your scratch paper,

159
00:07:21,656 --> 00:07:24,493
returns your things, and
dismisses you quietly,

160
00:07:24,513 --> 00:07:26,549
since others may still be testing.

161
00:07:26,584 --> 00:07:27,636
Now scores.

162
00:07:27,656 --> 00:07:32,350
College Board says most weekend scores
come out two to four weeks after test

163
00:07:32,370 --> 00:07:37,064
day, and it lists the exact release
date for each test on its score release

164
00:07:37,084 --> 00:07:38,029
dates page.

165
00:07:38,049 --> 00:07:40,997
You'll see them by signing in
to your College Board account.

166
00:07:41,017 --> 00:07:44,962
Your total score is on a scale from
four hundred to sixteen hundred.

167
00:07:44,982 --> 00:07:48,104
It's made of a Reading and
Writing score and a Math score,

168
00:07:48,124 --> 00:07:50,502
each from two hundred to eight hundred.

169
00:07:50,522 --> 00:07:51,522
One more thing.

170
00:07:51,772 --> 00:07:57,502
When you register for a weekend SAT,
you can send your scores to up to four

171
00:07:57,522 --> 00:08:00,323
organizations, like colleges, for free.

172
00:08:00,343 --> 00:08:05,467
And you have until nine days after the
test to use or change those free sends.

173
00:08:05,487 --> 00:08:08,201
So decide before that window closes.

174
00:08:08,242 --> 00:08:11,135
So, the short version.

175
00:08:11,349 --> 00:08:13,794
Exam setup done and ticket printed.

176
00:08:13,814 --> 00:08:15,400
A physical ID that matches.

177
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:16,722
Device charged.

178
00:08:16,742 --> 00:08:18,186
Phone put away.

179
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:20,098
Arrive by 7:45.

180
00:08:20,456 --> 00:08:23,865
Then use your tools, mark and
move, never leave a blank,

181
00:08:23,885 --> 00:08:25,873
and reset between modules.

182
00:08:25,893 --> 00:08:29,908
Next in this series: all
nineteen SAT math skills,

183
00:08:29,928 --> 00:08:31,678
explained one by one.

184
00:08:31,821 --> 00:08:33,515
If this helped, subscribe.

185
00:08:33,535 --> 00:08:34,928
Good luck on test day.
